# ============================================================================
# Environment variables — Pizzeria POS
#
# Phases 0–2 require NONE of these to build or run. The terminal runs against an
# in-memory mock DB driver + IndexedDB offline queue + PWA service worker, and
# EVERY PAYMENT RAIL FALLS BACK TO A SIMULATED SETTLEMENT WHEN ITS KEYS ARE
# ABSENT — so the full checkout flow (card, cash, crypto, split, refund, Connect
# onboarding, receipts) works end-to-end with ZERO env vars (incl. the Vercel
# preview). Provide a rail's keys to activate its REAL code path:
#   • STRIPE_SECRET_KEY        → real Stripe Terminal + online + Connect
#   • COINBASE_COMMERCE_API_KEY → real Coinbase Commerce charges
#   • BASE_RPC_URL             → real onchain USDC confirmation watcher
# All of these are OPTIONAL. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in when needed.
# NEVER commit real values — this repo is PUBLIC.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Supabase (schema in supabase/; driver in src/lib/db/supabase.ts) -------
# Setting NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + a key flips getPosDriver() from the
# in-memory mock to the LIVE Supabase driver — no code/call-site changes. Leave
# blank to stay on the mock (the zero-env default; build + tests pass with none).
# Apply the schema with `npm run db:apply` (DATABASE_URL set). See supabase/README.md.
# Public (browser) values:
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only. Bypasses RLS — never expose to the client. The driver reads it
# only server-side and always filters tenant-scoped queries by tenant_id.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# For psql / migrations / RLS tests (npm run db:apply, db:test:rls):
DATABASE_URL=

# ---- Stripe — Connect + Terminal + online (Phase 2) -------------------------
# OPTIONAL. With STRIPE_SECRET_KEY unset, the stripe_terminal + stripe_online
# rails and Connect onboarding all run SIMULATED (instant approval / instant
# "connected"). Set it to enable real charges on tenant connected accounts with
# application_fee. STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET verifies the Stripe webhook (no-op when
# unset). The publishable key is used by Stripe.js / the Terminal SDK on the
# client (Phase 4 online checkout).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Platform Connect / application-fee config:
STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID=

# ---- Platform fee — per-order Connect application_fee (Phase 2) -------------
# OPTIONAL defaults for the per-order platform fee taken off CARD charges via
# Connect application_fee_amount. Per-tenant overrides live in payment_settings
# (mock store settings today). Defaults: 250 bps (2.5%) + 10c flat.
PLATFORM_FEE_BPS=
PLATFORM_FEE_FLAT_CENTS=

# ---- Stripe Billing — OUR subscription revenue from tenants (Phase 6) -------
# OPTIONAL. This is how WE charge tenants a monthly subscription — entirely
# separate from Connect (the tenant's own card revenue). Billing runs SIMULATED
# unless STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (above) AND at least one tier Price id below are set;
# in simulated mode subscriptions live in the mock driver (trial → active) and
# the plan picker + gating + /platform billing all work with ZERO config.
#   • STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER / _PRO / _MULTI → the Stripe Price (price_…) for each
#     subscription tier; presence flips the tier to the REAL Checkout flow.
#   • STRIPE_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET → verifies the subscription-lifecycle webhook
#     (/api/billing/webhook). No-op (200) when unset.
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
STRIPE_PRICE_MULTI=
STRIPE_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- Platform admin (Phase 6) -----------------------------------------------
# Super-admin (/platform) auth is DEFERRED (Phase 7/Supabase). Today a seeded
# platform-operator identity drives the surface + audit log. No env vars are
# required; a real impl would check the authed user against `platform_admins`.

# ---- Crypto: onchain USDC on Base (Privy stack) (Phase 2) -------------------
# OPTIONAL. With BASE_RPC_URL unset, the crypto_onchain_usdc rail SIMULATES a
# pay-to intent that auto-confirms after a few seconds. Set BASE_RPC_URL to
# enable the real confirmation watcher (reads tx receipts from Base). PRIVY_*
# would mint per-order deposit addresses in production. USDC_*_ADDRESS overrides
# the USDC contract (defaults to USDC on Base mainnet). CRYPTO_PAY_TO_ADDRESS is
# the receiving wallet (the tenant's wallet) shown to the customer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=
BASE_RPC_URL=
USDC_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=
USDC_BASE_ADDRESS=
CRYPTO_PAY_TO_ADDRESS=

# ---- Crypto: Coinbase Commerce (Phase 2) ------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. With COINBASE_COMMERCE_API_KEY unset, the crypto_coinbase rail
# SIMULATES a hosted charge that auto-confirms. The webhook secret verifies the
# Coinbase webhook signature (no-op when unset).
COINBASE_COMMERCE_API_KEY=
COINBASE_COMMERCE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- Kitchen Display System — realtime + printer (Phase 3) ------------------
# ALL OPTIONAL. The KDS works fully with NONE of these set:
#   • Realtime: with no Supabase project, the board uses the POLLING realtime
#     provider (re-fetches /api/kitchen/orders on an interval). Wiring the
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values above swaps in Supabase Realtime behind the
#     same provider seam (src/lib/realtime/) — no component changes. Optional
#     override for the poll cadence (ms):
KDS_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=
#   • Printer: with KITCHEN_PRINTER_URL unset, kitchen tickets print via the
#     BROWSER print dialog (the /kitchen/ticket/<id> route). Setting it would
#     enable a network-printer dispatch (ESC/POS / CloudPRNT) behind the printer
#     seam (src/lib/printing/) — documented but NOT wired (no device in preview).
KITCHEN_PRINTER_URL=

# ---- Delivery providers (Phase 4) -------------------------------------------
# ALL OPTIONAL. Delivery works fully with NONE of these set:
#   • In-house manual: computes zone/fee/ETA from the location's store-config
#     delivery zones and queues each delivery for MANUAL driver assignment in
#     /admin — needs NO env, always "real".
#   • DoorDash Drive: with the three DOORDASH_* values UNSET, the provider
#     SIMULATES quote/dispatch/track (deterministic fee+ETA derived from the
#     zone, a simulated driver). Set all three to enable the REAL Drive API
#     (JWT-signed quote → accept → track). DOORDASH_BASE_URL overrides the API
#     host (defaults to https://openapi.doordash.com). Absence → simulated.
DOORDASH_DEVELOPER_ID=
DOORDASH_KEY_ID=
DOORDASH_SIGNING_SECRET=
DOORDASH_BASE_URL=

# ---- Customer accounts — magic-link sign-in (Phase 4) -----------------------
# No email provider is in scope: the magic-link account is SIMULATED. The
# sign-in link is RETURNED in the API response (and shown in the UI) instead of
# being emailed, so the account-claim flow is demoable end-to-end. No env vars
# are required; a real impl would wire an email provider and stop returning the
# token. The link is built from NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL (below) or the request
# origin when unset.

# ---- Observability (Phase 7) ------------------------------------------------
# ALL OPTIONAL. The app emits structured JSON logs and threads a request/trace
# id through API routes with NONE of these set.
#   • LOG_LEVEL: minimum log level (debug|info|warn|error). Defaults to `info`.
#   • SENTRY_DSN: when set, the error-tracking seam (src/lib/observability/errors)
#     routes captured errors to an external tracker; UNSET → structured-log no-op.
#     The Sentry SDK is intentionally not yet a dependency (live wiring deferred).
LOG_LEVEL=
SENTRY_DSN=

# ---- Training / demo mode (Phase 7) -----------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. TRAINING_MODE=1 (or running on the mock driver, the current default)
# marks the deployment as NOT taking real orders/money so staff can train. See
# docs/PRODUCTION_READINESS.md. Accepts 1|true|on|yes.
TRAINING_MODE=

# ---- App ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL of this deployment (used for callbacks/webhooks + magic links).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
